// P2/S2 (refinement-on-type): a refinement alias's interval now lives ON the
// type (Type.refine, cached by type_refine_interval) and is returned by
// type_integer_range — previously that query returned "unknown" for an alias.
// Here `Pos = i32 >= 1 and <= 9` carries [1,9] on its type, which excludes 0 and
// so discharges the `!= 0` divisor precondition with no runtime check.
// DECIDE-M (2026-09-28): a signed quotient needs one bit more than its operands — `a / b`
// with a possibly TYPE_MIN dividend over a divisor that may be -1 is 2^31, which no i32
// holds (and was a C division trapping at -O0, a silent value at -O2). The result is i64
// here so this test stays about what it tests: the divisor.
type Pos = i32 >= 1 and <= 9
func d(a i32, b i32 != 0) i64 { return a / b }
func f(n Pos) i64 { return d(100, n) }
func main() i32 { return 0 }
